{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a visible-light-induced, synergistic excited-state copper catalysis system using Cu(IPr)I and rac-BINAP. This method facilitates the carbo-aroylation of unactivated alkenes with aroyl chlorides, providing access to over 10 distinct classes of heterocycles, including tetrahydropyridoindoles and indoloisoquinolines. The reaction is applicable to late-stage diversification of complex molecules like peptides and natural products.",
